  "id": "tasks/a-failed-task-keeps-the-error-its-worker-s-turn-raised",
  "title": "A task whose worker's turn failed keeps the error the turn raised, its kind and its message, whether it failed before or after a tool round, inline or in the background, a transport shared into the child room or not; reported in the child room, the failure is marked so on the task",
  "rules": [
    "§23.3 step 6",
    "§6.4",
    "§10.6.5"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tests/tasks/test_task_turn_record.py::test_a_failed_task_keeps_the_error_its_turn_raised; tasks/models.py finished_task_fields (exception, error_reported), core/_turn_host.py _wait_task ({result, exception}, the exception as its error record). The provider refuses with status 503, an error it does not retry: a ProviderError, as in Python's test. first fails at its first generation, after once a tool round is done; each runs inline on the trace and with email shared, then in the background, delegated by boss's turn, whose host reads the failure itself. DelegatedTaskResult.exception is never serialized: only wait_task carries it, as an error record whose kind each implementation's codec writes (roomkit qualifies it with its module): the scenario reads the class's name in it. The record carries the error's attributes too (status_code 503 among them): tasks/a-failed-task-s-exception-keeps-its-attributes asserts them. A scripted model has one provider path: Python's buffered/stream parameter is not varied.",
